Find the equation of the parabola shown, which has vertex $(-1,4)$ and passes through the origin.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-4, xmax=3, ymin=-6, ymax=6, samples=100, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick={-3,-2,1,2}, ytick={-4,-2,2,4}]
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, <->, domain=-2.58:0.58] {-4*(x+1)*(x+1)+4};
\fill (axis cs:-1,4) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (axis cs:0,0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above] at (axis cs:-1,4) {$(-1,4)$};
\node[below right] at (axis cs:0,0) {$O$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
